# systemd presets for the Open AD Kit X5H image (issue #120 M7).
# Installed by aib/x5h-rootfs.aib.yml to /etc/systemd/system-preset/.
#
# This file enables six units: sshd, the role banner, two container mounts, the NPU service, and CR52 remoteproc.
#
# THE FIVE QUADLET UNITS ARE NOT LISTED, and adding them would be a no-op
# that reads like a decision. Quadlet generates their .service units at
# boot and writes the default.target.wants symlink itself for every
# .container that carries an [Install] section -- that is what "enabled"
# means for a generated unit, and no preset line adds to or subtracts from
# it. So awf-oak-{autoware,bridge,relay,restamp} come up at boot because
# their unit files say [Install] WantedBy=default.target, and
# awf-oak-simulator does not because it deliberately has no [Install] at
# all (a scenario must never run unbidden; see the note in that file). The
# only lever over that set is the unit files, not this file.
#
# rpmsg-eth.service IS installed by the manifest and is deliberately NOT
# enabled here -- a standing human ruling. Its daemon binary
# (/usr/local/bin/rpmsg-eth) is hand-staged per rpmsg-dualboot.md and is
# not in the image, so enabling it would put a unit in the boot path that
# cannot run on a freshly flashed board. It is not left unreachable by the
# omission: awf-oak-bridge.container carries Requires=rpmsg-eth.service, so
# the link is pulled up at boot on any board where the bridge starts, and
# the unit's own ConditionPathExists= makes an unstaged binary a skipped
# unit with one journal line rather than a failure or a restart loop.
#
# awf-oak-x5h-extract-map.service was enabled here until the nine-unit set
# was retired. Both the unit and the kashiwanoha map it extracted are gone
# (the MRM scenario ships its own matched map, staged onto the board by
# scripts/stage-scenario-map.sh), so the line was naming a unit that no
# longer exists and had to go with it.
#
# cr52-remoteproc.service is enabled now that its script ships in the
# image; on a board without a staged ELF it logs
# CR52_RPROC_SKIP reason=no_firmware and exits 0, and in the npu role its
# condition skips it. rpmsg-eth.service is still NOT enabled (standing
# ruling: its binary is hand-staged).
enable sshd.service
enable x5h-role-banner.service
enable var-lib-containers.mount
enable var-opt-npu.mount
enable x5h-npu.service
enable cr52-remoteproc.service
